# The Miskatonic Gazette / Widow's Bight Bureau, printing office.
# The town's civic narrative: editorial self-preservation dressed as arithmetic.
NPC: gazette_editor
LOCATION: business_district
SCHEDULE: morning=printer, midday=printer, evening=tavern, night=home

TOPIC: default
  GATE: NOT topic_done(gazette_editor, default) AND coat = plain
  TAG: editor_plain
  MR. HALLECK: "We're setting type for Friday's evening run."
  [The editor glances up from a tray of lead slugs, wiping ink from his knuckles.]
  MR. HALLECK: "If you have a business notice, give it to the boy at the front desk.\nIf you're here about the editorial on harbor dredging, save your breath."

TOPIC: default
  GATE: NOT topic_done(gazette_editor, default)
  TAG: editor_badge
  MR. HALLECK: "Officer Corwin. I saw your captain's dispatch on the club deaths."
  WALTER CORWIN: "Did Odell tell you what to print?"
  MR. HALLECK: "Captain Odell doesn't edit this paper, Officer.\nHe merely provides the facts the municipality is prepared to vouch for."

TOPIC: the_omitted_two
  GATE: evidence(eight) AND NOT evidence(gazette_correction_printed)
  TAG: editor_omitted
  LABEL: "Confront him about omitting the mother and boy"
  TIME: 5
  WALTER CORWIN: "Your morning edition reports six dead in a gas-main mishap.\nEight people died in that garden."
  MR. HALLECK: "Six subscribers died, Officer. Six prominent civic trustees whose obituaries take half a page each."
  WALTER CORWIN: "And the woman thirty yards away?"
  MR. HALLECK: "A colored woman and a minor with no local address, no coroner's identification, and no estate in probate.\nWhat headline would you have me set? 'Transients Perish Near Club'?"
  WALTER CORWIN: "They were murdered."
  MR. HALLECK: "A word like murder requires an indictment. A D.A.'s signature.\nOur District Attorney is currently lying on a marble slab in the precinct cellar."
  NOTEBOOK: editor_omitted_1 | "Miskatonic Gazette editor defended omitting the woman and boy from the reported count: 'Six subscribers died... A word like murder requires an indictment.'"
  EVIDENCE: press_suppression

TOPIC: press_the_arithmetic
  GATE: evidence(press_suppression) AND evidence(lay_lead) AND NOT evidence(gazette_correction_printed)
  TAG: editor_arithmetic
  LABEL: "Demand an honest retraction"
  TIME: 6
  FORK:
    CHOICE: "Threaten to name advertisers connected to the club."
      MR. HALLECK: "Go right ahead, Corwin."
      [He sets a heavy composing stick down on the marble imposing table with a flat clatter.]
      MR. HALLECK: "Josiah Pruitt owns the mortgage on this building. Corliss's firm writes our libel insurance.\nI have eleven men working those flatbed presses who have children to feed on Saturday. That isn't conspiracy. That's arithmetic."
      NOTEBOOK: editor_mortgage | "Pruitt and Corliss held the Gazette's building mortgage and libel bond; the paper cannot print allegations against the club."
      EVIDENCE: gazette_leverage
    CHOICE: "Describe Almy's account of the wage inquiry."
      MR. HALLECK: "A hundred-year-old whaler's claim from before the Civil War?"
      [He shakes his head, lighting a stub of a cigar.]
      MR. HALLECK: "Nobody in Miskatonic County buys a newspaper to read about century-old whaling debt.\nThey buy it to know which bank is solvent."
      NOTEBOOK: editor_lay_dismissed | "Gazette editor refused the Freeman wage claim as ancient history unsuited for news print."
      EVIDENCE: lay_publicity_refused

TOPIC: gas_main_origin
  GATE: evidence(press_suppression) AND NOT topic_done(gazette_editor, gas_main_origin)
  TAG: editor_gas_source
  LABEL: "Ask who suggested the 'gas-main' story"
  TIME: 4
  WALTER CORWIN: "Who gave you 'gas-main tragedy'?"
  MR. HALLECK: "Dr. Fenn's junior associate called before dawn, before the wagon even finished loading."
  WALTER CORWIN: "Before the coroner opened a skull."
  MR. HALLECK: "He said an accidental expansion of foul air in the lower conduit caused sudden asphyxia.\nIt sounded Latin. It sounded respectable. It filled the column."
  NOTEBOOK: editor_gas_origin_1 | "Dr. Fenn's associate phoned the 'gas-main/foul air' explanation to the Gazette before dawn, prior to any autopsy."
  EVIDENCE: fabricated_foul_air

# Shared inquiry: four different completed refusals make the question travel.
TOPIC: crew_omission
  GATE: topic_done(local_historian, crew_omission_official) AND NOT topic_done(gazette_editor, crew_omission)
  TAG: gazette_editor_crew_omission
  LABEL: "Ask why the town's history leaves out the crew's names"
  TIME: 3
  WALTER CORWIN: "Why does the town's history leave out the crew's names?"
  MR. HALLECK: "A commemorative column is not a passenger manifest."
  WALTER CORWIN: "They were the crew. Why leave their names out?"
  MR. HALLECK: "Because a column has a bottom, Corwin. Take your complaint to the Historical Society."
  NOTEBOOK: crew_omission_refusal | "Asked Mr. Halleck why the crew's names are missing from the town's history. No explanation supplied; the question remains open."

# An optional return inquiry: the counter's received pages change what he will print.
TOPIC: correction_terms
  GATE: evidence(press_suppression) AND evidence(naomi) AND NOT topic_done(gazette_editor, correction_terms)
  TAG: editor_correction_terms
  LABEL: "Ask what he needs to correct the count and print Naomi's name"
  TIME: 4
  WALTER CORWIN: "Mrs. Almy identifies the woman as Naomi Freeman. Will you print her name beside the count?"
  MR. HALLECK: "Her word, and what else?"
  WALTER CORWIN: "She keeps a meal ledger."
  MR. HALLECK: "Then copy the entry. Put the identification and its source into a report the precinct has received. Bring those pages back."
  WALTER CORWIN: "You would print eight?"
  MR. HALLECK: "As the number in your received report. No murder weapon, no culprit, no sermon. A correction with a source."
  NOTEBOOK: correction_terms | "Halleck will consider a sourced correction: eight deaths, Almy's identification of Naomi, and her meal-ledger entry must be in received report pages. Copy the ledger at the boardinghouse, file any later discoveries as a precinct supplement, then return to the editor."
  EVIDENCE: gazette_correction_terms

TOPIC: correction_pending
  GATE: evidence(gazette_correction_terms) AND NOT (filed(eight) AND filed(naomi) AND filed(lodging)) AND NOT topic_done(gazette_editor, correction_pending)
  TAG: editor_correction_pending
  LABEL: "Ask whether the correction can go ahead yet"
  TIME: 0
  MR. HALLECK: "The count, the identification, and the ledger entry, Corwin. All in received pages. Your notebook is yours; it is not the precinct's receipt."
  NOTEBOOK: correction_pending | "Halleck still requires the count and both identification sources in received paperwork. A discovery made after filing needs a dated supplement."

TOPIC: print_correction
  GATE: evidence(gazette_correction_terms) AND filed(eight) AND filed(naomi) AND filed(lodging) AND NOT topic_done(gazette_editor, print_correction)
  TAG: editor_print_correction
  LABEL: "Lay out the received pages and request the correction"
  TIME: 8
  [Halleck lays the received pages side by side. His finger stops on the entry from Almy's book.]
  MR. HALLECK: "The first heading remains six."
  WALTER CORWIN: "Read the pages underneath it."
  [He turns the page. Then he draws a rule across a scrap of copy paper.]
  MR. HALLECK: "Eight reported deaths. Naomi Freeman, identified by the boardinghouse keeper and her meal record. Cause unestablished. That is what these pages support."
  WALTER CORWIN: "Print that."
  [The small proof press gives a dry knock. Halleck sets a narrow correction slip beside the morning paper.]
  THE GAZETTE — CORRECTION: "The received police report records eight deaths at the Ophion estate. Mrs. Almy identifies the woman as Naomi Freeman; her meal ledger corroborates the account. The boy's name remains unestablished. No cause has been established in the report."
  MR. HALLECK: "This goes with the copies still on the counter. I can't call back the ones already sold."
  NOTEBOOK: printed_correction | "Collected a printed Gazette correction slip: eight reported deaths; Naomi Freeman identified by Almy and corroborated by her ledger; boy unnamed and cause unestablished. It accompanies unsold copies. The original six-person edition and captain's heading remain unchanged."
  EVIDENCE: gazette_correction_printed
